%S A401223 1,12,53,224,892,3420,12704,45864,161992,562912,1930312,6545496,
%T A401223 21988784,73296272,242715784,799199592,2618729664,8544429216,
%U A401223 27775440600,89993963896,290735590480,936801729264,3011431024040,9659788306440,30925102957280,98825979115968
%N A401223 Number of largest sets S of points of the 3 X n grid such that any two distinct rectangles with all four corners at grid points (tilted rectangles included) have distinct sets of corners outside S.
%C A401223 Sets are counted as subsets of the grid, not up to symmetry. A rectangle with all four corners in S has the empty set of corners outside S, so at most one rectangle can be hidden in this way.
%C A401223 a(n) = A399580(3,n) for n >= 2. The largest size is A397315(3,n) = n+2 for n >= 3.
%C A401223 For n >= 3 every such set has one point in each column, except for either one column with all three points, or two columns with two points each whose two row pairs are different. Of the n^2*3^(n-1) sets with this column structure, the fraction counted here tends to 4/27.
%H A401223 Arjun Pemmasani, <a href="/A401223/b401223.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%H A401223 Peter Kagey, <a href="https://peterkagey.com/problems/001/">Open Problem Collection, Problem 001</a>.
%H A401223 Arjun Pemmasani, <a href="https://github.com/apemm/Kagey-Problems/blob/main/kagey-problems/problem001/jis/pemmasani.pdf">Maximum Blackouts That Keep Every Lattice Rectangle Identifiable</a>, preprint, 2026.
%H A401223 Arjun Pemmasani, <a href="https://github.com/apemm/Kagey-Problems/tree/main/kagey-problems/problem001">Solvers, exhaustive verification, and pre-registration ledger for Problem 001</a> (GitHub repository).
%H A401223 <a href="/index/Rec#order_15">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (15,-93,317,-702,1188,-1512,972,144,-1136,2640,-1104,-800,-576,-3456,-1728).
%F A401223 G.f.: (x - 3*x^2 - 34*x^3 + 228*x^4 - 641*x^5 + 1307*x^6 - 2186*x^7 + 2056*x^8 - 236*x^9 - 1060*x^10 + 2584*x^11 - 4264*x^12 - 1440*x^13 + 704*x^14 - 1024*x^15 + 2080*x^16 + 2176*x^17 + 384*x^18)/((1-3*x)^3*(1-2*x-2*x^2)^3*(1+2*x^2)^3).
%F A401223 a(n) = 15*a(n-1) - 93*a(n-2) + 317*a(n-3) - 702*a(n-4) + 1188*a(n-5) - 1512*a(n-6) + 972*a(n-7) + 144*a(n-8) - 1136*a(n-9) + 2640*a(n-10) - 1104*a(n-11) - 800*a(n-12) - 576*a(n-13) - 3456*a(n-14) - 1728*a(n-15) for n >= 19.
%F A401223 a(n) = 4*(n-1)*(3*n+2)*3^(n-5) + E(n) for n >= 4, where E(n) > 0 counts the sets counted here that contain the top and bottom points of some column.
%F A401223 a(n) = (4/81)*n^2*3^n - (4/243)*(n+2)*3^n + O(n^2*(1+sqrt(3))^n).
%e A401223 a(3) = 53. Fifteen of the sets have a column with all three points. Twenty-eight have two columns with two points, with row pairs {1,3} and one of {1,2}, {2,3}. Ten have two columns with two points, with row pairs {1,2} and {2,3}. One of the sets (1 = in S, rows numbered from the top):
%e A401223   1 1 1
%e A401223   1 0 0
%e A401223   1 0 0
%o A401223 (PARI) my(x='x+O('x^30)); Vec((x - 3*x^2 - 34*x^3 + 228*x^4 - 641*x^5 + 1307*x^6 - 2186*x^7 + 2056*x^8 - 236*x^9 - 1060*x^10 + 2584*x^11 - 4264*x^12 - 1440*x^13 + 704*x^14 - 1024*x^15 + 2080*x^16 + 2176*x^17 + 384*x^18)/((1-3*x)^3*(1-2*x-2*x^2)^3*(1+2*x^2)^3))
%Y A401223 Row 3 of A399580.
%Y A401223 Cf. A001787, A397315, A401224, A401225, A401226.
